course: dictionary
lesson: 2528
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning separately, and the sentence around the word shows you which one to use. «Decorator» is one of these words. It can mean a person who paints and wallpapers rooms, or someone who makes things look beautiful, like a cake decorator.
explain: Look for clues. «Decorator crabs stick bits of sponge and seaweed on their shells to hide» is about animals, so the word here means a creature that decorates its own shell. There are no rooms or cakes in that sentence, so the house meaning does not fit.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. If it mentions walls, rooms, or wallpaper, the word means a painter. If it mentions code or a function, it means a Python feature. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A decorator can be a person whose job is painting and wallpapering rooms and houses (UK).
fact: A decorator can also be someone who decorates things, such as a cake decorator or an interior decorator.
fact: In computing, a decorator is a special code feature, used in languages like Python, that adds behaviour to a function.
fact: «Decorator crabs» stick bits of sponge and seaweed on their shells to hide.
fact: The plural of decorator is decorators.
exercise: Ella hired a decorator to paint her bedroom and hang new wallpaper. What does decorator mean here? | *A person who paints and wallpapers rooms | A piece of computer code | A cake maker who adds icing | A crab that covers its shell
exercise: «Decorator crabs stick bits of sponge and seaweed on their shells to hide.» What does decorator mean in this sentence? | *A creature that decorates its own shell to hide | A piece of computer code | A person who paints walls
exercise: In a Python lesson, what is a decorator? | A person who builds chips | A tool for painting walls | *A special code feature that adds behaviour to a function | A kind of crab
test: The decorator crab changed its decorations when it moved to a new place. What did it change? | *The bits of sponge and seaweed on its shell | Its name | Its home on the sea floor | Its colour, like a cuttlefish
test: In «builders and decorators for one house», what does decorators most likely mean? | Fish that match the sea floor | Computer programmers | *People who paint and wallpaper rooms | Cooks who make cakes
exam: Jayden reads «decorator» in a Python book and in a house-painting advert. Why do the meanings differ? | *Because the context tells you which meaning fits | Because the word changes its spelling | Because the dictionary is wrong | Because the word has only one meaning
